1
00:00:00,625 --> 00:00:01,251
[PAUL]
Jao!

2
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:01,835
- Sir?
- How are you?

3
00:00:01,876 --> 00:00:04,169
What are you doing here?
Why didn't you tell me?

4
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:07,715
Our CEO acquired a new property
here in Barangay Cabitoonan.

5
00:00:07,716 --> 00:00:09,050
Barangay Cabitoonan…

6
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,927
The one next to the
mangrove plantation?

7
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:11,969
Yes.

8
00:00:11,970 --> 00:00:13,471
And you’re the project lead!

9
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,264
I can’t be part
of this project, sir.

10
00:00:15,265 --> 00:00:16,850
How could you be
the project head?

11
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,477
I honestly had no idea they’d
make me project head for this.

12
00:00:19,519 --> 00:00:21,104
That's how my boss works.

13
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,731
Without those mangroves,

14
00:00:22,772 --> 00:00:26,233
Typhoon Odette would have
hit the island even harder.

15
00:00:26,234 --> 00:00:28,653
So please, come
with me tomorrow.

16
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:31,196
Those trees aren't just trees.

17
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:33,115
They're protecting
our community.

18
00:00:33,116 --> 00:00:34,617
[MAN]
Don't worry, ma'am.

19
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:36,035
We'll help you.

20
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,579
[ARIEL]
You’re awfully quiet.

21
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:38,580
What’s going on with you?

22
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:41,207
I’m already helping you out!
I don’t even work here!

23
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,333
[JAO SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Good morning.

24
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:46,379
We're here to hear your
thoughts on the luxury resort.

25
00:00:46,421 --> 00:00:47,297
[OLD LADY]
You two look good together.

26
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:48,631
[CROWD GIGGLING]

27
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:49,549
We're very different.

28
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:50,633
[PAUL]
Kara, right?

29
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,177
I’m Paul.

30
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:53,720
Jao’s boss.

31
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,221
Five million?

32
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,140
10 million.

33
00:00:57,390 --> 00:00:58,683
[PAUL]
Name your price.

34
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:03,563
Leave gracefully.

35
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,733
Or I’ll expose your
company for bribery.

36
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:09,194
Company?

37
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:11,905
The company that’s giving
your boyfriend a good life?

38
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:14,615
So I’m assuming…

39
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:18,453
you can’t do for Jao what
you did for your ex, huh?

40
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:21,206
We're not going to
poison the waters.

41
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:23,248
We're not going to
displace communities.

42
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:24,167
In fact,

43
00:01:24,209 --> 00:01:27,378
we're gonna give this
community opportunities.

44
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:29,214
Opportunities to thrive.

45
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:30,507
Jobs.

46
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,717
My relationship is
none of your business.

47
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:36,512
And protecting the environment
is even more important.

48
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:39,349
This is the community
the mangroves will protect.

49
00:01:41,935 --> 00:01:43,728
You know,
in this digital age?

50
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:47,440
News travels fast.

51
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:50,944
We wouldn't want
people to find out that…

52
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,613
you were the face
of your ex's company.

53
00:01:55,031 --> 00:01:56,740
You know, bribing...

54
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:58,867
all these certain communities

55
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,870
for their crimes against
the environment?

56
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:02,705
What if that news goes out?

57
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,749
What does that make you?

58
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:06,918
A hypocrite?

59
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:10,171
And what about Jao?
Poor guy.

60
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,050
The laughingstock
of the community?

61
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:17,303
You should think about that...

62
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:19,681
Ms. Caitlyn De Leon.

63
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:21,140
That's your name, right?

64
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:25,270
You know,
me and Jao go way back.

65
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:27,939
[PAUL SCOFFS]

66
00:02:28,106 --> 00:02:29,524
But that doesn't matter.

67
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:31,943
Here's my advice for you.

68
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:35,071
You could change your name,

69
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:37,239
you could change
your lifestyle,

70
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,242
your personality…
everything!

71
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,119
But remember this.

72
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:46,040
The past will always
come back for you.

73
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:47,959
It will hunt you down.

74
00:02:56,593 --> 00:03:01,055
[ALON BY JL]

75
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,210
[JAO]
Mica, Architect Zulueta,

76
00:04:12,251 --> 00:04:15,129
thank you so much for agreeing
to be part of my rogue team.

77
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:18,633
[MICA ON VIDEO CALL]
I believe in your vision, sir.

78
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,175
[ZULUETA ON VIDEO CALL]
Anything for you, Jao.

79
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:22,303
I still owe you a beer and sisig.

80
00:04:23,012 --> 00:04:26,015
Seriously, though.
I believe in your girlfriend's cause.

81
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:29,769
But I understand that you don’t want to
jeopardize your position in Young Horizon.

82
00:04:30,269 --> 00:04:31,603
Of course, Architect, but...

83
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:34,190
that's why we need to come
up with a win-win solution

84
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:36,818
for the company and
the people of Siargao.

85
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:40,612
[MICA ON VIDEO CALL]
Sir, you know this is risky if Sir Paul finds out.

86
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:42,615
That's why it's just
the three of us, Mica.

87
00:04:42,657 --> 00:04:44,658
Because I trust you
both 100 percent.

88
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:46,953
[MICA ON VIDEO CALL]
Why are you really doing this, sir?

89
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:49,622
For the island or for Kara?

90
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,251
“Boat.”

91
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,130
But seriously, I'm…

92
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:59,382
Long story,
but to cut it short…

93
00:05:00,758 --> 00:05:03,052
I'm doing this to protect
what matters to me.

94
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:07,056
Kara and the island.

95
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,143
They're one and the same.

96
00:05:18,484 --> 00:05:20,445
[INFLUENCER ON VIDEO]
This Kara really got some nerve

97
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,362
acting like she’s some
environmentalist island girl.

98
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:25,366
Turns out, she has a past
darker than my enemy's armpit.

99
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:27,201
So she really is
Caitlyn De Leon.

100
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:30,705
Remember, that social climber accused
of bribing an Indigenous community

101
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:33,833
that were victims of environmental
crimes committed by her ex?

102
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:34,459
Oh...

103
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,502
[PHONE RINGING]

104
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:37,545
Release it.

105
00:05:38,629 --> 00:05:40,380
Make sure it’s
during peak hours,

106
00:05:40,381 --> 00:05:41,715
all at once,

107
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,135
with all the influencers
on your payroll.

108
00:05:45,136 --> 00:05:46,137
Got it?

109
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:01,902
This suits you, too.

110
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:03,236
[CUSTOMER]
Will that look good on me?

111
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,739
Yeah, with your skin tone.

112
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,491
[ARIEL SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Oh, my god!

113
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,993
Sorry.
I'm sorry.

114
00:06:09,827 --> 00:06:12,330
[SIARGAONON]
I’m not okay, Kara!

115
00:06:14,123 --> 00:06:15,124
Come here.

116
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:16,375
Thank you.

117
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:18,503
Oh, thank you!
Thank you.

118
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:20,004
Look at this.

119
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:22,006
Oh!

120
00:06:22,007 --> 00:06:23,466
- [CUSTOMER] Hi! Excuse me.
- Hi!

121
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:24,175
Yes, please come in.

122
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,593
Over here.

123
00:06:28,888 --> 00:06:30,932
[INFLUENCER ON VIDEO]
So, guys, judge for yourselves

124
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:36,520
whether she really cares about
Mother Nature and the mangroves.

125
00:06:36,521 --> 00:06:40,525
And look at all these comments!
Of course, they're anonymous.

126
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,568
“She's just an outsider,

127
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:45,113
so she doesn't care
about the island's future.”

128
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:47,406
“Exactly.
She’s just hiding.”

129
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:48,615
"Hypocrite."

130
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:51,743
“She only used the island
for her own interests.”

131
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:52,953
"She's overstaying."

132
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:55,873
“She should go back to
wherever she came from.”

133
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:01,212
These are peak hours for
social media engagement.

134
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:02,547
[ARIEL CLICKS TONGUE]
Gosh.

135
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:06,676
Jao's boss isn't even trying to
hide his dirty tricks anymore, huh?

136
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:09,053
I'm just impressed by
how fast they pulled this off.

137
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:12,722
And they really seem to know
their way around dirty tactics.

138
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:15,059
I honestly thought
he was a decent guy.

139
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:18,604
And people on social
media are so quick to judge!

140
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:21,357
I can't really blame them.

141
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,235
They've only heard
one side of the story.

142
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,112
Exactly.

143
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:29,698
I don't know if you'll agree,
but I think...

144
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:33,119
people need to hear
your side of the story.

145
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:37,915
With all due respect, sir,
stop bullying Kara.

146
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,209
[PAUL ON THE PHONE]
What are you talking about?

147
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,461
I know you're
behind the black ops.

148
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:45,338
Your fingerprints
are all over

149
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,717
this online smear
campaign against her.

150
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:51,012
[PAUL ON THE PHONE]
Jao, isn’t this just SOP?

151
00:07:51,053 --> 00:07:54,807
When someone is being stubborn,
we hire someone to dig up dirt on them.

152
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:57,268
They fold.
The project pushes through.

153
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:58,603
Nothing new.

154
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:00,061
I never approved any of this.

155
00:08:00,062 --> 00:08:01,897
[PAUL ON THE PHONE]
But you never complained before.

156
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,940
Not until now.
Because of Kara.

157
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:05,943
Well, don't be so complacent, sir.

158
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:08,154
Kara's different.

159
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:11,240
After everything
she's been through,

160
00:08:11,490 --> 00:08:13,492
she's tougher
than a mangrove.

161
00:08:14,493 --> 00:08:16,704
You won't bring
her down that easily.

162
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,214
[ARIEL]
Are you ready, Kara?

163
00:08:35,348 --> 00:08:38,976
Everything said about
me in the viral video is true.

164
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:45,233
I was once involved in
a project that harmed...

165
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,902
not only the environment,

166
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,739
but also the lives
of many people.

167
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:57,203
I admit that I was wrong
to support that project.

168
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,832
And I deeply regret it.

169
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:05,461
[KARA BREATHES DEEPLY]

170
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:07,296
But I'm here now,

171
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:10,299
not to clear my name,

172
00:09:11,342 --> 00:09:14,345
but to fight to protect
the environment

173
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:17,890
and the future of the
people here in Cabitoonan.

174
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:22,436
We can't stop the
storms from coming.

175
00:09:23,729 --> 00:09:26,440
But we can
reduce the damage

176
00:09:26,732 --> 00:09:29,235
and devastation they cause.

177
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:33,364
I'm asking you all

178
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:37,910
to stand up for the
mangroves that protect us

179
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,788
from the destruction
brought by these storms.

180
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:47,962
And to Young Horizon,

181
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:51,841
who continue to bully me,

182
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:55,219
I didn't simply hide here.

183
00:09:56,762 --> 00:10:00,474
The people of this island
welcomed me and took care of me.

184
00:10:01,475 --> 00:10:02,685
And now,

185
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:05,730
I want to stand up for them.

186
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:10,026
As a representative
of the NGO Pure Coast,

187
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:14,572
I will be filing a Motion for Mediation
with the Coastal Protection Office.

188
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:18,242
I'll see you in
the proper venue.

189
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:20,161
Thank you.

190
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:54,570
You didn't inform me you
were going to do a livestream.

191
00:10:56,364 --> 00:10:58,157
Do you realize how
dangerous that was?

192
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,700
You’re only exposing
yourself more.

193
00:11:00,701 --> 00:11:02,828
I told you I'd handle it.

194
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,039
My enemy is your ally.

195
00:11:05,498 --> 00:11:07,500
Why would I tell you my plans?

196
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:10,461
Can I remind you that
I'm on your side here?

197
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,964
I'm just trying to protect you.

198
00:11:15,007 --> 00:11:16,801
I can handle myself, Jao.

199
00:11:20,262 --> 00:11:22,973
You might as well just
say you don't need me.

200
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,725
I need you, Jao.

201
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:28,354
But not for the
reasons you think.

202
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:44,828
[JAO] Sir, I have received the
plans and all the community reports

203
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,663
and environmental
reports as well.

204
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:50,251
And after receiving the data,
I have to admit…

205
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:52,086
Kara’s right.

206
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:55,673
Preserving the mangrove
plantation is still the priority.

207
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,217
[BOSS] I've seen the
appeal on the viral vlog.

208
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,928
Apparently, the Coastal Protection Office
is going to sue us?

209
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:03,388
Sir, um...
don't worry about that.

210
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:05,683
I've got this all
under control, okay?

211
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,934
And the...

212
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,812
Environmental Certificate of Compliance
should be granted soon.

213
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:10,980
So, we'll get that soon.

214
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:12,897
So let's just leave her alone.

215
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:13,899
Please.

216
00:12:13,941 --> 00:12:17,027
Our project, our luxury resort,
will be built as scheduled.

217
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,070
I promise.

218
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:20,697
Um...

219
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:24,117
Sir, I think we have to
consider looking into alternatives

220
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,036
on how we can
develop the area.

221
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,622
[BOSS]
Jao, what are you saying?

222
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,666
There are other ways

223
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,293
to protect the mangrove site

224
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:35,296
and at the same time,
still build the resort

225
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:38,674
that can provide growth, jobs,
and opportunities within the area

226
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:40,926
without destroying
the ecosystem.

227
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:42,428
So I'm proposing...

228
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:47,223
that we should build a sustainable
eco-resort in Cabitoonan.

229
00:12:47,224 --> 00:12:48,684
But, sir, you know...

230
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,144
[BOSS]
Let's hear it from Jao.

231
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:54,398
Honestly, Paul, you should've
thought of a better alternative first.

232
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:56,859
Plan it right away, Jao.

233
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,740
[NOAH] We've been
researching for days now.

234
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:05,951
Almost 24/7,
digging into Young Horizon.

235
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:08,787
But it looks like all their
projects are above board.

236
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:13,042
Apparently, Jao's boss
runs a clean operation.

237
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:15,877
But if they're up
to anything shady,

238
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:18,088
I'm sure we'll find a crack.

239
00:13:18,547 --> 00:13:21,842
[NOAH] But, Kara, I hope
you’re aware that if we do find dirt,

240
00:13:22,301 --> 00:13:25,513
your boyfriend could get
caught up in the exposé.

241
00:13:27,181 --> 00:13:32,520
[PHONE RINGS]

242
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:33,812
Hello?

243
00:13:35,272 --> 00:13:36,273
Yes.

244
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,028
Oh, okay.

245
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,073
Okay, thanks.

246
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:51,205
Young Horizon just posted an
announcement on their website.

247
00:13:51,622 --> 00:13:53,748
They're pivoting on the project.

248
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:55,751
So instead of a luxury resort,

249
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,796
they're changing it to
an eco-friendly resort.

250
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:01,215
And they want to
consult and work with us.

251
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:02,841
- Is that true?
- It's for the mangrove sanctuary...

252
00:14:02,883 --> 00:14:04,593
that they want
to build within it.

253
00:14:07,429 --> 00:14:09,223
Yes.
Confirmed.

254
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:21,652
[JAO]
Another free meal for you.

255
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:23,779
- [TANTAN CHUCKLES]
- [JAO] My treat!

256
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:25,406
What's the occasion,
Sir Handsome?

257
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:27,449
What’s with the treat?

258
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:30,285
Nothing.

259
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,495
I'm just happy, Tantan.

260
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:33,288
Everything's going to be okay.

261
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:34,498
You’re right.

262
00:14:35,749 --> 00:14:37,960
You and Ms. Kara won't
be fighting anymore.

263
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:40,963
I hope so.

264
00:14:42,381 --> 00:14:44,174
But what about you, Tantan?

265
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,635
Never thought about...

266
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,762
leaving the island?

267
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,181
Hm...

268
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:53,726
I know a lot
of people who have.

269
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:57,313
But me?

270
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:59,982
No.
I'm happy here.

271
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:03,360
Never thought about how
much better your life could be...

272
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:04,945
if you tried to go to Manila?

273
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,114
Maybe.

274
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:09,491
But what's there for me?

275
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:12,036
Would I be happy there?

276
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,039
Hm...
I don't know.

277
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,582
But I know one thing.

278
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,375
I'm happy here.

279
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:20,419
What about you,
Sir Handsome?

280
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:22,796
Still planning to
go back to Manila?

281
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:25,758
We're still developing
the eco-resort, right?

282
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:27,635
And after that?

283
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,470
You're leaving again?

284
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:34,350
No.

285
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:37,936
I’ll grow old here in Siargao.

286
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,483
Kara and I will
build our family here.

287
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:48,489
That's a big one.

288
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,450
You're the best, Pining!

289
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,744
- One more. I’m out.
- [TANTAN] Delicious.

290
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:59,124
[ARIEL]
Kara, Sir Noah.

291
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:00,959
- [KARA] Hello.
- [ARIEL] Have some snacks.

292
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,086
[ARIEL] It’s pan de coco.
(Sweet coconut-filled bread)

293
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,796
- Thank you.
- Thanks, Ariel.

294
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:06,131
You're going to
need some fuel

295
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:09,176
because things are
getting intense here.

296
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:11,095
[KARA SIGHS]

297
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:12,763
[NOAH]
Kara.

298
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,223
Look at this.

299
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,642
Headquarters is asking
for your contact info.

300
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:20,979
They want to offer you the
international field officer position.

301
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,607
[NOAH]
This is great, Kara!

302
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:25,150
This is a great opportunity.

303
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:30,698
Is that the one...

304
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:32,533
with headquarters in Denmark?

305
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:33,574
Yeah.

306
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:34,702
[ARIEL]
Denmark?

307
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,621
You're going
international, Kara!

308
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:44,211
But if I accept it,
do I have to leave the island?

309
00:17:10,821 --> 00:17:11,947
[KARA]
You know, Jao…

310
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:16,451
I was willing to expose the
irregularities of your company.

311
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,245
You could've just asked
me yourself, you know?

312
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:19,872
I know where all
the dead bodies are.

313
00:17:19,913 --> 00:17:22,915
I really don't know why
you're taking this so lightly.

314
00:17:22,916 --> 00:17:24,126
Let’s not…

315
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:27,045
Let’s not dwell on things
that haven't happened yet.

316
00:17:27,087 --> 00:17:28,672
[PEARL]
OMG! OMG!

317
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:30,299
- [PEARL] OMG!
- What is it?

318
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:33,218
Ariel, I got accepted!
I got the scholarship!

319
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,052
[PEARL GIGGLES EXCITEDLY]

320
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:35,471
Wow! Congratulations!

321
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:37,014
[SIARGAONON]
We’re going to celebrate!

322
00:17:37,055 --> 00:17:38,932
Wait, I just need to
do something, okay?

323
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:40,142
Hi, Sir Han!

324
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:43,270
Thank you for believing in me.

325
00:17:43,312 --> 00:17:44,897
But I also hate you.

326
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:48,650
I hate that you're not answering
my calls or my messages.

327
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:49,942
[CAROL]
Pearl...

328
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:51,236
Be strong, okay?

329
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:52,571
[CAROL SPEAKS SIARGAONON]
Be strong.

330
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,198
[ARIEL]
Take care, Princess Pearl

331
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,741
[CAROL CRIES]
